Upstream code in the other patches. A patch script under patches/mpv,
patches/ffmpeg or patches/rubberband quotes lines of the source of mpv, FFmpeg
or Rubber Band to find where it applies, and may write code into those files.
The quoted lines stay code of that project, under its license (mpv and FFmpeg:
LGPL-2.1-or-later; Rubber Band, only in the GPL build: GPL-2.0-or-later), and
so does every file a patch writes or changes in an upstream source tree. The
code of this repository that a patch adds to such a file is BSD-3-Clause, and
in the patched file it goes with that file, under its license. Code of mpv or
FFmpeg that a file of this repository adapts (not only quotes) is
LGPL-2.1-or-later, and that file is listed above.

The libraries the scripts build are under the license that README.md
("Licenses") names: LGPL-3.0-or-later, or GPL-3.0-or-later when built with
LIBMPV_GPL=1.
